<title>USA: U.N. okays two more Iraqi contracts, Russians buy.</title>
<headline>U.N. okays two more Iraqi contracts, Russians buy.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A pair of Iraqi crude oil contracts for Russian buyers were approved by U.N. overseers Thursday morning, according to a U.N. spokesman.</p>
<p>Iraq has received approval for 16 contracts out of a total 22 submitted to the overseers. The U.N. said the total barrel volume for the approved contracts is 83.52 million barrels.</p>
<p>The U.N. does not give the length of the term contracts, and whether the deals apply to only the first period of the 180-day accord.</p>
<p>Following is an updated list of the contract volumes and nationality of the receiving company:  </p>
<p>Contract No. 1 - 5.5 million barrels/Russian</p>
<p>Contract No. 2 - 6.12 million barrels/French</p>
<p>Contract No. 3 - 2.7 million barrels/Italian</p>
<p>Contract No. 4 - 13.5 million barrels/Turkish</p>
<p>Contract No. 5 - 3.6 million barrels/Swiss</p>
<p>Contract No. 6 - 3.6 million barrels/U.S.</p>
<p>Contract No. 7 - 1.8 million barrels/Turkish</p>
<p>Contract No. 8 - 5.4 million barrels/Spanish</p>
<p>Contract No. 9 - 5.4 million barrels/French</p>
<p>Contract No. 10 - 7.2 million barrels/Russian</p>
<p>Contract No. 11 - 3.6 million barrels/U.S.</p>
<p>Contract No. 12 - 10.8 million barrels/Dutch</p>
<p>Contract No. 13 - 1.8 million barrels/Austria</p>
<p>Contract No. 14 - 4.4 million barrels/Morocco</p>
<p>Contract No. 15 - 5.5 million barrels/Russian</p>
<p>Contract No. 16 - 2.6 million barrels/Russian</p>
<p>Iraq is allowed to sell $2.14 billion worth of crude from June 8 to Dec 6. The deal requires Iraq to export up to $1 billion in two separate 90-day periods, the first one ending on Sept 5.</p>
<p>((--Patrick Connole, NY Oil Desk, +1 212 859 1828))</p>
</text>
